Id suggest that you replace Pathworks on the 5000 with Samba and upgrade
the PCs to Windows for Workgroups (or Win95). Samba is a freeware Lan
Manager implementation that is *wonderful*. It does file/print services,
understands long file names, etc. It compiles out of the box for Ultrix
(and a bunch of other Unix systems as well). The ftp site is
nimbus.anu.edu.au in pub/tridge/samba. If you use Windows for Workgroups,
you need to get the tcp stack from Microsofts ftp site (free also).  

