In article <1995Nov28.000738.15865@nosc.mil>, 
blombard@nosc.mil (Bob Lombard) writes:

> I've got a situation where I need to be able to make copies of a 
> set of TK85 tapes on a regular basis.  Does any one know of any 
> available off-line or stand-alone duplicators ?

> If not.. any one have any experience in doing tape to tape 
> duplication using 2 drives on a machine ?

Assuming that you are running VMS, why not use VMSTPC to
copy the tapes?   VMSTPC will make a disk file that is
an image of any arbitrary tape, then spit out as many identical
copies as you like.   I have even used it to make copies
of 4mm backup tapes from a PC!

It also has the advantage of being *VERY* fast!   The PDP-11
version that it was modeled on started out as a test to see
how fast you could run a tape drive.

VMSTPC is available on the DECUS CDROMs and Symposium Tapes.

