Just fyi, the 3000 was a "DEC 3000".  The new naming convention since 
summer 1994 is roughly:

     AlphaMumble x y/z

where

     Mumble = Server or Station
          x = cabinet size
                  200 = desktop  (250 is same but bigger cache)
                  400 = deskside (narrow) 
                  600 = deskside (wider)
                 1000 = microwave
                 2000 = two microwaves
                 2100 = 2 drawer filecab (but deeper)
                 8200 = shallow refrigerator
                 8400 = big refrigerator
          y = chip generation 
                    4 = 21064 or 21064A (dual issue)
                    5 = 21164 (quad issue)
          z = approximate Mhz (usually exact, but occasionally rounded
                               to a number that doesn't seem "odd" to
                               marketing) 

