>Hi!
>
>I'm a beginner of Digital Unix 3.2C. Please teach me how to
>increase harddisks.

I don't understand the question, but I'll take my best guess.

To add new devices, you add them to the bus, shutting down if
necessary, and then use /dev/MAKEDEV to create the special device
file.  With the special device file, you can then label the disk
with the disklabel command and use it.

The "add them to the bus" part depends a lot on the particular
system being used.  Most systems support SCSI, which is fairly
simple, but others use a backplane RAID controller that has to
be setup using standalone utilties.  Also, SCSI based subsystems
such as the RAID Array 410 have their management commands to
add disks and construct arrays.  And, there are still a few
MSCP disks still around.

>What's commad like 'format' on SunOS?

I think much of what Sun does in "format" is provided by
disklabel.  This will let you write an initial label to
the disk and then customize the partition table if desired.

To do a low level device format (rarely needed) you can use
the scu(8) command for SCSI disks.

