>   An AS400 has software built in to emulate sna and rje services.  I have 
> defined an AS400 as a node in jes for transfering reports. On the AS400 the 
> mvs jes is defined as a task running under qsnads subsystem. A terminal can 
> use 3270 emulation (pf keys get all mixed up though), but if you can swing 
> it I'd recommend using a pc and running a terminal emulation. I think Rumba 
> is now part of pc support now (or client support if it's 3.5) which does a 
> nice job.   
> 
There is a difference between RJE (Remote Job Entry) and NJE (Network Job 
Entry). 
We have both RJE and NJE running. We use the RJE for submitting JCL streams to 
the MVS host. WE use NJE for transmitting network files vis the MVS command 
TSO TRANSMIT (from themainframe). You can also use SNDNETF (Send Network File) 
 for transmitting files to the MVS host from the AS/400.
Use the CFGDSTSRV (Configure distribution Services) command on the AS/400 to 
create a distribution queue and routing table. I know you have to create a PU 
(Physical unit) on the MVS side to connect with a control unit on the AS/400 
side. 




