Sounds like a similar problem that I've had with my 1972 Mercury's
heater/AC fan circuit... it kept blowing fuses and melting the
connector that connects to the blower-motor switch (the motor isn't
drawing too much current).  Since it's such a pain to get to anything
under the dash of this car, I decided to take it to a Lincoln-Mercury
dealer to have it repaired a few years back, expecting to have the
problem properly repaired.  Guess what the geniuses did?  They simply
replaced the fuse with a circuit breaker.  Ah well... that just goes
to prove that if you want something repaired properly these days,
you've got to repair it yourself.

I know that this isn't DEC related, but if anyone else here has a 1972
to 1974 (plus and minus a few years to cover all cars in that line)
Mercury Montego or Gran Torino, please examine your heater/AC fan
wiring near the switch... those switch assemblies and connectors are
becoming difficult to find, and you could be at risk of your car
catching on fire.  We've got a '73 and a '74 as well from this line of
cars, and they've also had a similar meltdown problem.


