Dan Senderowicz (senderow@diva.EECS.Berkeley.EDU) wrote:
: The disk (190 MB) of my microvax (ba23) went dead, so I'm
: thinking on buying a new 1GB (or 2GB) that I've seen advertised
: ranging between 200 and 500 bucs (my controller is a RQDX3). Can
: I buy any IDE disk (seagate, quantum, etc.) besides DEC? If so,
: I would really appreciate any hints on the recommended settings
: (disktab, partitions, etc.) as well as the procedure. Thanks a
: lot.

Dan-

I believe that the RQDX3 is an ST-506 controller, rather than an
IDE controller.  Especially if it came with your MicroVAX II in a
BA-23.  You can tell by looking at the back of the drive.  If there
are two cables, one wide and one narrow, it is either ST-506 or
ESDI.  I'm not aware of any Q-Bus IDE controllers.

At this point, acquiring an ST-506 drive larger than about 400MB,
even used, would be virtually impossible.  If you really want to
upgrade, I would suggest looking at CMD or Emulex for their Q-Bus
SCSI controllers.  We have had a great deal of success using them
with VAXstation 3200 machines for a number of years.

Brett




