>>I have two problems with Pathworks:

 :

>We had the same gripe on a similar platform.  We use a 4400 and after a few
>manual "tweaks" to the GBLPAGES and GBLSECT parameters in SYSGEN, we 
>get consistent 270 KBps throughput. 

These two SYSGEN params are NOT known to directly have any performance impact.
They are just upper limits to specific system resources and will cause a 
failure when depleted, but will not give more performance when in ample supply.

While it is conceivable that a product adapts its way of working based on the
availability of gblpages, gblsections, I have yet to hear about a product
that does so to opt for a more performant application algoritmes. Products
I know require an application specific knob to be turned first in order to
be able to exploit more glbpages. For example, RMS can be allowed to open
more files with more global buggers if there is more slack in gblpages,
but the application wil need to issue a SET FILE/GLO=nn first (or provide
a clever FAB$W_GBC between $OPEN and $CONNECT).

