>#endif).
>On a DecAlpha is there a predefine command so that I can enter "#ifdef
>decalpha". Is decalpha exists ? if not what is the right name ?

You forgot to mention the operating system.  From your mention of RS6000
it can be assumed that you're interested in OSF/1.  If this is the case,
use:

    #if defined __alpha && defined __osf__

If you're sure your code will be never compiled under other Alpha OS, you
can use the simpler:

    #ifdef __alpha

In general, when you want to find out which symbols are predefined on a Unix
cc, try the -v compiler option, like this:

    cc -v foo.c

