dreid@wat.hookup.net (David Reid) wrote:
>Hi.
>
>My company is running a Microvax 3100 and VMS 6.0.
>I need some help with trying to change the print quality or font on an
>LA600.  What I want to do is be able to set the printer to run Letter
>quality for some forms and just draft mode for others.  I know you can
>send some print control info to the printer using the setup option for
>the define form command.  Unfortunately, I have not been able to find
>how to enter control codes to change the font or print quality of the
>printer.  When I tried to enter what I thought might be valid control
>sequences, I got an error that the library module was not found.  Is
>this the device control library?  Where is it and how can I find out
>what is in the library now?  If anyone can provide some help for this
>problem, I would really appreciate it.
>
>Thanks
>
>
>

Well, device control libraries are text libraries (.TLB files) created
with the library/create/text command.  I doubt that VMS has the 
controls for an LA600 in the standard library.  Anyway you can, using 
your printer docs create your own device control library.  Just put 
the control sequences for each setup into separate files. One for
each setup.  You shoud give each a meaningfull name. The use the 
library command to create the .TLB.  Place the library in 
sys$common:[syslib].  Use this library on the init command when you 
create the print queue.  Now the name of each control module (see 
library/list) can be used with define/for/setup or print/setup.

