keywords: Turbochannel VME grasshopper MVIA MVIB 3VIA
reply-to: jorge@sp071.cern.ch (Jorge Gomes)
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


  I'm trying to connect one VAXstation 4000-90 and one VAXstation 4000-90A
running VMS 5.5-2 to one VME crate with two "grasshoppers" Turbochannel to
VME interfaces also known as DWTVX-Ax composed of two boards one Turbochannel
card 3VIA (DWTVX-AA) and a VME card MVIB (DWTVX-AB). 

  We are using this setup to transfer data from a VME processor card (FIC8234 
with two 68040 processors running OS9) to the VAXstations using DMA. The 
handshake is very simple the VAXstations write in the FIC8234 fifos using
PIO to signal that they are ready to receive data, the FIC8234 does the DMA
to the VAXstation and signals the end of the transfer with a VME interrupt. 
  With this approach we are transferring data at 2.4 MB/s sustained rate.  

  I have some problems with this setup namely the VAXstations have lots
of hangs (they even don't respond to the reset switch). The VAXstation
4000-90 compared with the 4000-90A is by far the one with more hangs
(sometimes 4 hangs per day).

  The VAXstation 4000-90 is the boot member of a small cluster composed
by 2 satellites the VAXstation 4000-90A and a VAXstation 4000-60 (the
4000-60 doesn't have any Turbochannel to VME interface).

  Some weeks ago I saw a patch VAXSYSL18_U2055 that states the following:

  o  Due to changes in the timing on some TURBOchannel hardware, the
     VAXstation 4000 Model 90 and the VAXstation 4000 Model 60 may
     hang when certain TURBOchannel options are accessed after a
     reset.
  o  The VAXstation Model 90 hangs when the VME B board is accessed
     after reset.

  I've installed this patch and the CSCPAT_1045013 in the VAXstation 
  4000-90A. The CSCPAT_1045013 is required because VAXSYSL18_U2055 specifies 
  the following: 

     *********************** VAXSYSL18_U2055 **********************
     *  If you are going to install this ECO kit on a VAXstation  *
     *  4000 Model 60 or VAXstation 4000 Model 90 system that has *
     *  a TURBOchannel device installed *AND* is a member of a    *
     *  VAXcluster, you *MUST* install CSCPAT_1045 on your        *
     *  system either before or in the same installation session  *
     *  with this ECO.  If this ECO is installed on a             *
     *  system that meets the requirements mentioned above,       *
     *  the system will crash at boot time with an INVEXCEPTN     *
     *  bugcheck at STACONFIG+578A if CSCPAT_1045 does not        *
     *  exist on the system.                                      *
 
  After the installation of this 2 patches I'm experiencing crashes at
boot time probably due to VME interrupts (INVEXCEPTN bugcheck above
ASTDEL). In fact the system doesn't hang any more instead of hangs now
I have bugchecks.

        CPU 00 -- SSRVEXCEPT, Unexpected system service exception
        Process currently executing on this CPU:   None

  My questions are:
  1) Can VAXSYSL18_U2055 be installed in a 4000-90A ? I didn't installed it
     in the VAXstation 4000-90 because I don't want to have an Unbootable 
     boot member...
  
  2) Can VAXSYSL18_U2055 be installed in a satellite of a VMS cluster ? or 
     must it be a boot member ?

  3) Are this hangs more frequent in the VAXstation 4000-90 due to the fact 
     that the VAXstation 4000-90 is a cluster boot member ?

  4) Where can I get information regarding the SYSLOA49.EXE image and about
     the way it handles the Turbochannel to VME interface (3VIA / MVIB) ?
     I suspect the VAXstation hangs we are experiencing are really 
     related with the error handling done by this image !!!

  5) What are the differences between a VAXstation 4000-90 and a VAXstation
     4000-90A besides the speed ? 
     Why does the 4000-90A have much less hangs ?
     Is it just because of being faster than the 4000-90 ?  

  6) Why am i having this bugchecks ? I notice at least once a VMERST 
     entry in the errlog.sys at the same time of a crash, is this VMERST
     the source of the hangs (now bugchecks) ?
          
  7) When the cable between the 3VIA (Turbochannel board) and the MVIB
     VME board is disconnect the VAXstation also hangs, Is this hang
     related with the other "expontaneous" hangs ????
     I suspect this two kind of hangs are produced be the lost of clock 
     signal in the YABUS (the bus that connects the VME card to the 
     Turbochannel card) or by some other hard error. This error condition is
     detected by the error handler (sysloa49 ????) and probably a MVIB 
     reset signal is asserted until the presence of clock signal is detected. 
     Maybe something is going wrong while or after the MVIB reset is done ???  

  8) Is anyone out there having the same problem ?????

  Thank you
  Jorge Gomes 



