If I remember correctly, CSCPAT_1045 fixes a bug in STACONFIG causing 
the crash when third party TURBOchannel boards are installed.  (It also 
fixes some problems with the VAX 4000-100.)

We have CSCPAT_1045 V1.2 installed and have had no problems.  It is 
installed on all nodes, including our boot node.  It can be installed 
by itself.  I suspect that it just needs to be installed before 
VAXSYSL18_U255.

[snip]

>  8) Is anyone out there having the same problem ?????

I don't know if it is the same procblem or not, but we found that when 
our TURBOchannel board (a BCT-2100) was installed in a VAXstation 
4000-60 sattelite, we needed to set the SYSGEN parameter

    NISCS_LOAD_PEA0 = 1

or the system would crash when booting.  This problem did not occur if 
the machine was a boot node.

Good luck!

