X-Deja-AN: 119655411
references: <48i46e$ktq@server1.ctc.com>
organization: Sensor Systems
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec

Anthony Salony (salony) wrote:
: Can anyone tell me how I can change the default depth for the root window to 8
: planes, I am not having any luck doing this. Any help would be greatly
: appreciated.

You can specify a visual class for the root window at the time the X server
is started.  See the -cc and -class options in the Xserver manual page.
This allows you to change the visual class to pseudocolor which will
have the side effect on 24-bit displays of switching it to 8 bits as
there are no depth-24 pseudocolor visuals defined.

Note that your Xserver is almost certainly started with the "xdm" program
(this is the case if where you type your login and password is already
a window).  To change the Xserver options that XDM uses, you will need
to add them to the line in the file /var/X11/xdm/Xservers.  You then need
to get rid of the existing server and make XDM reread the file.  The
simpler way to do this is to just reboot, but you can also do
	/sbin/init.d/xdm stop

and then log into the console and do...

	/sbin/init.d/xdm start; logout

(The logout is to make sure your console login goes away after X starts).

-Ron




