What are you doing to test speeds?  Just compiling?  If you are doing
something disk intensive, and the disk subsystems are comparable, then
that's to be expected.  Compiles are fairly disk intensive, usually.
Lots of .c or .cpp files, .h files, temp files, .o files, .a files who
knows what.  Not a lot of computation there.

Do this.  Pop up the performance monitor and monitor the processor(s).
Watch how much the processor(s) work while you compile.  Do the same
thing on the P90.  Just for grins, you might turn the diskperf stuff
on and monitor disk activity as well.

On processor intensive activities, that Alpha should smoke a P90.

