From: altitude@nic.hq.cic.net (Alex Tang)
Subject: Alpha keeps panic'ing
Date: 1995/11/14
Message-ID: <48a5ad$1h2@news.cic.net>
X-Deja-AN: 119363274
organization: CICNet, Inc.
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec,comp.unix.osf.osf1

Hi folks.  I've got an Alpha (Dec 3000, OSF1 V2.0) that just started
panicing on a regular basis.  It's paniced and rebooted itself 10 times
since november 8.  Prior to this, we haven't had any major problems, and
we've had the machine for about 14 months.

The only major changes in the past 6 months or so was we put a new disk in
about 5 weeks ago.    I've included 2 of the 9 crash logs from
/var/adm/crash-data.  Crashes 0-3 have crash-data files that look like the
first example.  Crashes 4-9 have crash-data files that look like the
second example. 

From what I can tell, it's some sort of hardware problem that makes me
think "disk".  It looks like it keeps dying in one of the vm/swap
functions.  Can someone help me?

Thanx.
...alex...

