In article <1995Nov4.195215.214@mediatex.ch>, pn@mediatex.ch says...
>
>I have two problems with Pathworks:
>
>When I copy a big (10-20 MB) file from the PC harddisk to a VMS file service,
>sometimes it times out in the creation phase of the file. And the file is
>not copied. It's just allocated on the VAX but nothing is copied.
>I think, there is sum kind of timeout which is set to low, but I don't know
>what value I have to change.
>
>Second problem, when I copy files form PC to the VAX or otherwise, I get
>only poor (50-100 kBps) throughput. I know, ethernet has a physical capacity
>of 1000 kBps minus overhead should give at least 500 kBps throughput.
>When I copy the files to a NT server (Intel 80486-33 Based!) I get 200 kBps
>without a problem!
>What can I do to increase the troughput?
>
We had the same gripe on a similar platform.  We use a 4400 and after a few
manual "tweaks" to the GBLPAGES and GBLSECT parameters in SYSGEN, we 
get consistent 270 KBps throughput.  The basic install procedure gives you just 
enough to get going, and AUTOGEN can't compensate well enough.  Since we
have plenty of memory in the 4400, we kicked the GBLPAGES up to around 51000,
and the GBLSECT were doubled if I remember right.  Make sure that you update
SYS$SYSTEM:MODPARAMS.DAT with some MIN_'s so that AUTOGEN won't reset
them on you.




