>One other thing - recently, I've noticed a sort of acrid-like smell
>coming from the system at times.  I've tried sniffing around to see
>where it was coming from, but the sniff tests proved inconclusive,
>and everything was working fine.  Does the power controller usually
>produce an acrid smell before it begins behaving as noted above?

Check the BA23 power-harness: pull the front cover off, you'll find
the harness on the rifght. Pull the harness off and check the
connections. The older type - grey cable/orange connectors - were
prone to burning out with that very distinctive acrid smell. They
should be replaced with the newer type - red and black cables/white
connectors, cost a couple of pounds/dollars. If this turns out to be
the fault I can dig a part number out for you. You may still have a
power controller fault but you need to check for this problem before
sorting the power controller out.

