OK. That's what I would expect. Incoming mains is applied to the neon 
(note it's before the breaker - DEC normally did that), then to the 
breaker, the unswitched outlets, and the input of the contactor. The 
output of the contactor feeds the switched sockets. J1-2 and J1-3 provide 
a mains feed for the transformer on the control board. Shorting J1-2 to J1-1
will energise the contactor coil and then turn on the uswitched outlets

