>I have a 2 port SCSI controller with 3 external drives that I'm
>trying to get configured. The drives are 1 2 gig hawk, 1 2 gig
>barracuda, and a 4 gig hawk.

>Anyways, when I reboot back to the normal boot partition the drives
>go away. a 'T tc2 cnfg' shows them now as rz100a, rz200a, and rz300b.
>I've tried MAKEDEV to create these (as well as the rz25,rz27,rz35) and
>they create ok, but the system still doesn't see the drives. I can
>newfs them or mount them. It's almost as if the system did not put them
>into the device table at startup. Am I missing something? A device driver
>or something that's on the CDROM for the SCSI controller that might not
>be on the internal boot disk?
>

It would be useful to know what version of what operating system
you're running.  For ULTRIX, the dual channel SCSI controllers
aren't supported, but the PMAZB may work.  They do need some particular
configuration file work that wouldn't have been done if the device
wasn't present when the system was installed.

For Digital UNIX all the dual channel controllers are supported,
but again you may have to add line to the configuration file to
get it to work.  For later versions (V3.0+) all you need in the
configuration is lines for the controller.  The driver will figure
out that there are disks there and will take care of the rest.
--
