Robert> Anyways, when I reboot back to the normal boot partition the
Robert> drives go away. a 'T tc2 cnfg' shows them now as rz100a,
Robert> rz200a, and rz300b.  I've tried MAKEDEV to create these (as
Robert> well as the rz25,rz27,rz35) and they create ok, but the system
Robert> still doesn't see the drives. I can newfs them or mount
Robert> them. It's almost as if the system did not put them into the
Robert> device table at startup. Am I missing something? A device
Robert> driver or something that's on the CDROM for the SCSI
Robert> controller that might not be on the internal boot disk?

Read the man page for 'doconfig'.  What you need to do is tell the
kernel that it has this new SCSI controller so it can use the new
devices.  The basic method is as follows, though read the doconfig man
page!

1. shutdown to single user mode.
2. cp /genvmunix to /vmunix
3. shutdown to console mode
4. boot to single user mode.
5. mount /usr
6. /usr/sbin/doconfig
7. follow the instructions to build a new kernel
8. mv the new kernel from it's build location to /vmunix
9. shutdown to console mode
10 boot the system to multiuser mode.




