In article <47t43o$rpf@omega.ludd.luth.se>,
John Vestberg <john@ludd.luth.se> wrote:

>> Ultrix runs on all VAX series machines.
>
>Not true. Not on my MicroVAX 3100-40.

Ultrix does not support
	. the NVAX chip used in many post-1991 VAX products
	. the SOC chip (the SOC is almost identical to the CVAX
	chipset, but there are differences and even if the rest
	of the system were identical to a supported VAX the kernel
	would still require changes)
	. the SPX graphics processor

There is also some other hardware it doesn't support, or doesn't support
on VAXes even though it does on MIPS.  I think the general rule is any VAX
built after 1991 can't run Ultrix.


-- 
    John Carr (jfc@mit.edu)



