Anthony Salony (salony) wrote:

: I need to change the default window depth to 8 planes from 24 planes and can
: not find any instructions on how to accomplish. Does anyone know how to change
: the default window depth? Any help would be grealty appreciated.

There isn't a good way to change the depth, but you can changed the class
look at the -cc and -class options to the Xserver.  Since the 8 bits are
usually psuedocolor and the 24 bits are usually direct color, this probably
will get you what you want.  It would be nice if there was better control
of this, but that's X for you.  What other client-server application has no
way of matching the errors up with the requests :-).

