What does the command 'mt status' report?  And doing 'mt offline'
doesn't eject the tape either?

One option is to do a system shutdown, power off the tape drive (and
the rest of the system), push and hold the eject button, then turn
power back on to the tape drive.  This should force the system to
eject the tape, but if it doesn't then you have really serious
problems and will have to get field service to look at the drive.

If you can't shutdown the system, you can try opening the case and
just unplugging the power to the tape drive, then plug the power back
in while holding down the eject button.  If nothing is accessing the
tape drive at the time, then you should be all set.

