In article <55hh0in623.fsf@igor.physics.wayne.edu>, Dale Atems <atems@physics.wayne.edu> writes:

>
>Sorry if this has been asked recently, but does anyone have a disktab
>entry for the ST410800N (the 9GB Elite series drive)?

For most uses, you don't need a disktab entry on ULTRIX or Digital
UNIX (I'll assume you're asking about one of the two).  On Digital
UNIX the disklabel command and on ULTRIX the newfs command can get
the geometry and default partition table from the driver.

On Digital UNIX, once labeled, newfs will use the geometry information
that is in the label and a disktab entry isn't needed.  On ULTRIX you'll
need to customize the partition table for this disk since it is limited
to 2 GB file systems.

Unfortunately, disklabel doesn't have an easy way to get the correct
rotational speed (even if it isn't interesting).  If you plan to need
it you can edit the label to put in the correct value.
