If you compile your source files with the "-migrate" switch, you also
need to link with that switch.  For example, if you compile like this:

	% cc -c -migrate foo.c

You should link like this:

	% cc -o foo -migrate foo.o

The "-migrate" switch causes the linker to include files from the "libots.a"
library.  This library contains support routines needed for the gemc_cc
compiler.

The other libraries you found (libFutil.a, libUfor.a, libfor.a) are support
libraries used by the Fortran compiler.

