<478sg5$3a6@tweedledumb.cygnus.com> ian@cygnus.com (Ian Lance Taylor)
writes:

Ian> bkort@musenet.org (Barry Kort) writes:
>> Ian Lance Taylor (ian@cygnus.com) wrote:

>> : I have a DECstation 3100 with no hardware manuals.  For a while now,
>> : when it boots, it counts down from 7 to 2 and then reports a failure.
>> : Nothing much else seems to go wrong, so I've been ignoring it.

>> You don't say what the line of "gibberish" is...

Ian> It doesn't give one.  When I turn the machine on, it counts down from
Ian> 7 to 2, and starts blinking FAILURE on and off and waits for the
Ian> machine to be reset.  When I push the reset button, it counts down
Ian> from 7 to 2 again, again prints FAILURE, and then goes to the boot
Ian> monitor.

This means your LANCE ethernet interface is starting to die.  You can
run some more tests on it from the console with:

	t e	(ESAR)
	t L	(Lance)
	t n	(Net RAM)

Then replace the appropriate FRU, which is the motherboard.  The going
rate these days seems to be around $300-500 for a replacement
motherboard.

