ORACLE run the TPC C benchmarks on the DEC 8400 ALPHA system last week. 
The results were impressave to say the least. The  actual numbers were:

9414 tpmC TPC-C 
$316 per tpmC

The system was the fastest ever tested running the ORACLE database. The 
cost per tpc was the lowest for any high performance system. The system 
consisted of 8GB of mem and 8 CPU's [DEC ALPHA 21164 chip]. some 
compairson numbers are the HP9000 t500 which ran at  5369 tpmC and $535 
per tpm.  This was with 12 CPU's. The  benchmark clearly showed the power 
of 64 bit processing and very large mnemory.

The cost per tpm figure includes the 5 year system cost. Purchase price of 
hardware and software, 5 year hardware and software support, all I/O, etc.

This was a  fully TPC compliant audited and public disclosed benchmark, 
so the numbers can be belived.

