REQUEST FOR VOLUNTEERS

The DECUS U.S. Chapter is currently engaged in a process that will lead to 
a revised Digital program at our national events.  We are looking for users 
to volunteer to act as a "sounding board" as to what you think of possible 
program content.  This would involve attending a weekday two-day meeting in 
late November or mid December to meet with senior Digital folks to discuss 
the design of sections of the Digital program at the St. Louis event.  
DECUS will fund your travel expenses for this meeting. After the meeting 
you will be asked to comment on material either via e-mail or a conference 
call.

If you are an interested user who is responsible for managing or leading 
the implementation of the types of applications scenarios below, using 
Digital products or services, please send me e-mail (killeen@decus.org) or, 
you know of someone please also send me e-mail.

	3-Tier C/S computing.

	Distributed transaction processing.

	High performance UNIX data servers.

	Managing a corporate data warehouse.

	Electronic commerce with 3rd party transaction processing.

	Deploying applications using WNT as a enterprise server.

	Moving applications from OVMS to WNT or UNIX.

	Continuing to deploy and manage OVMS systems and applications.

	Managing heterogeneous systems and networks.

Again we looking for folks who are deploying new applications or who have 
just deployed applications in the above scenarios using Digital platforms.  
Your involvement will help build a better program for yourself and all 
DECUS members.

