: I have a regular dial-in account to a Unix running Ultrix.  I want to
: set up a slip/ppp connection so I can run Netscape.  Is there a program
: out on the 'net that will allow me to set up a slip/ppp connection?

It is possible to configure SLIP or PPP into an Ultrix kernel.  You 
have to have root on the machine and you have to know how to rebuild
the kernel.  SLIP is in the Unsupported Subsets.  PPP is available
from public FTP sites.  If you've never done this before, expect
to spend a few days learning how.

Barry



