: I have a DECstation 3100 with no hardware manuals.  For a while now,
: when it boots, it counts down from 7 to 2 and then reports a failure.
: Nothing much else seems to go wrong, so I've been ignoring it.

You don't say what the line of "gibberish" is...

On *VAXstation* 3100, an unterminated Ethernet gives this message:

	?? 1  0C00	0000.7004

Check the cables, connectors, and terminators.  Test the system
with a single section of known good ethernet cabling and terminators.
It could be a marginal cable with some poor impedance matches.

